        The gauge measures everything pushing on the tank wall. It does not know which gas is doing
        the pushing. Before anyone clears this system, prove how much of that pressure belongs to
        hydrogen.

  - id: after-total
    on: { after: [1, 2] }
    presentation: [nearby_character_bubble, equipment_panel_update, persistent_world_change]
    world: >-
      On the equipment panel, hydrogen particle icons move faster than nitrogen particle icons at
      equal temperature; the total-mole estimate appears beside the pressure gauge.
    stage:
      wall:
      - text: 'SAME TEMPERATURE = SAME KINETIC ENERGY'
        tone: ok
      - text: 'TOTAL GAS: 406 mol'
        tone: warn
    panel: 'TOTAL GAS: 406 mol'
    panelTone: warn
    bubbles:
    - who: herrera
      say: >-
        The total amount is plausible. That still does not make it usable hydrogen. Sample the line
        from the tank to the reactor.

  - id: after-sampling
    on: { after: [3] }
    presentation: [nearby_character_bubble, equipment_panel_update, persistent_world_change]
    world: >-
      The tank and regulator remain hydrogen-rich, but the reactor branch turns yellow as nitrogen
